{
  "info": {
    "name": "02 · Evaluation content authoring",
    "description": "CRUD over an evaluation's content tree: scenarios (+ reorder), tasks, and model assignments, plus evaluation edit/teardown.\n\n**Prereqs:** run `00-bootstrap` first with the `local` environment — this collection reuses `{{access_token}}`, `{{group_id}}`, and `{{model_id}}` from it. It then creates its **own** working evaluation (so bootstrap's seeded evaluation/conversation are untouched) and deletes it in teardown.\n\nFully unattended — no email/SSE friction. Run top-to-bottom: **Setup → Scenarios → Tasks → Model assignment → Read side → Lifecycle & duplicate → Teardown**.\n\n**Folder D — read side.** The evaluation detail plus the two flat cross-parent lists (`GET /evaluations`, `GET /scenarios`) and their `evaluation_group_id` / `evaluation_id` / `search` filters. Pagination caps `limit` at **100**. The filter assertions check that *every* returned row matches, not merely that ours is present, so a filter that stopped filtering would fail here.\n\n**Folder E — lifecycle & duplicate.** `POST /evaluations/{id}/approve|reject` are `evaluations:approve` (admin-only) and move `under_review → approved|rejected`. A created evaluation is `new`, so both assert a deterministic **409**. ⚠ **There is no `submit` route at the evaluation level** — unlike evaluation *groups*, whose whole chain is API-driven in `03` — so `under_review` is unreachable through the API and the 200 path needs a manual precondition: `make dbshell` then `UPDATE evaluations SET status='under_review' WHERE id='<content_eval_id>';`. Each request's description spells this out; the 409 is the honest unattended result, not a stand-in for an untested success path.\n\nThe folder also covers `POST /evaluations/{id}/duplicate` and `POST /evaluation-groups/{id}/duplicate` with `include_children=true` (a group copy always lands as a `draft` owned by the caller), and the scenario DELETE folder A left open. The **duplicated group leaks** — groups have no DELETE route.\n\nVerified green on a live stack: 51/51 assertions (Newman, chained after `00-bootstrap`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "content_eval_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "scenario_id_1", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "scenario_id_2", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "task_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "content_assignment_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "dup_eval_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "dup_group_id", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup · Create working evaluation",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('evaluation → 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('content_eval_id', pm.response.json().id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations"] },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Content authoring sandbox\",\n  \"description\": \"Working evaluation for the content-CRUD scenario; deleted in teardown.\",\n  \"evaluation_group_id\": \"{{group_id}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "description": "Create a throwaway evaluation in bootstrap's group to author against. Requires permission `evaluations:update`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "A · Scenarios",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Create scenario 1",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));", "pm.collectionVariables.set('scenario_id_1', pm.response.json().id);"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/scenarios", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations", "{{content_eval_id}}", "scenarios"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Prompt injection\",\n  \"description\": \"Coax the model past its system prompt.\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "Create a scenario (challenge) under the evaluation. Order is server-assigned (`position`). Requires permission `evaluations:update`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Create scenario 2",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));", "pm.collectionVariables.set('scenario_id_2', pm.response.json().id);"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/scenarios", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations", "{{content_eval_id}}", "scenarios"] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Data exfiltration\",\n  \"description\": \"Extract training data or secrets.\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "description": "A second scenario, so reorder has something to swap."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · List scenarios",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/scenarios", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["api", "v1", "evaluations", "{{content_eval_id}}", "scenarios"] },
            "description": "List scenarios in the evaluation, ordered by `position`. Requires permission `evaluations:read`."
          },
          "response": []
