                  "pm.test('search narrows rather than widens', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().items.every(i => /content/i.test(i.title) || /content/i.test(i.description || ''))).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations?search=Content&limit=100",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "evaluations"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "Content"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The `search` filter is a case-insensitive `ILIKE` over **`title` OR `description`** (`services/evaluations.py`), not the title alone \u2014 so the assertion accepts a match in either field. Asserted as \"every row matches\" rather than \"ours is present\", so a filter that silently stopped filtering would fail here."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 · List scenarios across evaluations",
          "event": [
