    {
      "name": "E · Lifecycle, duplicate & scenario delete",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 · Approve from the wrong state → 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('names both states', () => { const d = pm.response.json().detail; pm.expect(d).to.include('new'); pm.expect(d).to.include('approved'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/approve",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "evaluations",
                "{{content_eval_id}}",
                "approve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`evaluations:approve` (admin-only). The transition is `under_review → approved|rejected`, and a freshly created evaluation is `new`, so this is a **409** — the deterministic, unattended outcome.\n\n**⚠ Reaching the 200 needs a manual precondition.** There is no `submit` route at the *evaluation* level (unlike evaluation **groups**, which have the full `submit`/`approve`/`request-changes`/`reject` chain — see `03`), so `under_review` cannot be reached through the API at all. To see the success path:\n\n```\nmake dbshell\nUPDATE evaluations SET status='under_review' WHERE id='<content_eval_id>';\n```\n\nthen re-run this request and expect 200 with `status: \"approved\"`. The 409 asserted here is the honest unattended result, not a stand-in for an untested success path."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 · Reject from the wrong state → 409",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/reject",
              "host": [
