            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"rejection_reason\": \"Out of scope for this engagement.\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Same source-state rule and the same `dbshell` precondition as step 1. `rejection_reason` is required on the reject body and is persisted onto the evaluation."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 · Duplicate the evaluation with its children",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('dup_eval_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('the copy is a fresh row', () => pm.expect(b.id).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('content_eval_id')));",
                  "pm.test('and starts at status new', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('new'));",
                  "pm.test('it lands in the same group', () => pm.expect(b.evaluation_group_id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('group_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluations/{{content_eval_id}}/duplicate?include_children=true",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "evaluations",
                "{{content_eval_id}}",
                "duplicate"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "include_children",
                  "value": "true"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "`evaluations:create`. `include_children=true` deep-copies the scenarios, their tasks and the model assignments; runtime data (conversations, flags, reviews) and credentials are **never** copied."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 · The copy carries the scenarios",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('children came across', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().items.length).to.be.at.least(1));",
                  "pm.test('and belong to the copy, not the source', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().items.every(i => i.evaluation_id === pm.collectionVariables.get('dup_eval_id'))).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/scenarios?evaluation_id={{dup_eval_id}}&limit=100",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "scenarios"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "evaluation_id",
                  "value": "{{dup_eval_id}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "What `include_children` actually did — copies, re-parented to the new evaluation."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5 · Duplicate the parent group (children included)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('→ 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('dup_group_id', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "pm.test('the copy is a draft', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('draft'));",
                  "pm.test('carries an author (single identity here, so caller-vs-source needs a two-identity run)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().created_by_id).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/evaluation-groups/{{group_id}}/duplicate?include_children=true",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "evaluation-groups",
                "{{group_id}}",
                "duplicate"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "include_children",
                  "value": "true"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The group-level duplicate (`evaluation_groups:create`). The copy always lands as a **`draft`** owned by the caller, whatever the source's status — so a template can be cloned and reworked without touching a published engagement.\n\nThe caller must be the source's **owner** or hold the `evaluation_groups:manage` break-glass — merely being able to *see* a group is not enough to clone it. A since-soft-deleted owning organisation is dropped rather than carried as a dangling reference."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6 · Delete the duplicated evaluation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
